  identity: "an_unreached_effect_leg_reads_as_one_that_ran_and_refused" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungUnread { cause: BlockerClassUnstated },

  receipts: [
    "**an unreached effect leg reads as one that ran and refused** (a remote effect whose transport never reached the host -- ssh could not connect, so no remote shell began -- is reported with the same value as a leg whose script ran and refused, so the caller can neither retry the first without retrying the second nor resume the leftovers the first one strands).",

    "INVALID STATE: retired gunbc.spark.pair_serving_apply (deleted #13779) SparkPairHostApplyOutcome had two arms, Applied and Failed, and every non-zero session result became Failed. ssh(1)'s own 255 (extdeps.ssh.session ssh_client_error_exit_status) was folded into the script's refusal exits.",

    "HARM: fleet-converge run 36918167575 (2026-10-01, mode spark_v41_group_a_launch). One leg to srv7 timed out over Wi-Fi (`ssh: connect to host 192.168.1.232 port 22: Connection timed out`), the whole four-host transaction rolled back, the rollback leg to srv7 timed out too, and srv7 kept `.gunbc-had-no-unit` and `.gunbc-transaction`. Every later run refused at preflight until a human deleted them. A transient link loss cost a full arm abort plus a manual intervention.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: whether a remote shell reported BEGINNING. That wrap now lives in gunbc.spark.host_privileged_apply spark_pair_leg_payload (extracted from the deleted pair_serving_apply); spark_pair_leg_outcome_of reads Unreached only when neither line arrived AND ssh exited 255. A began-line with no exit line is a script that RAN to an unknown point and is Failed, never retried. stderr text is not the discriminator (gunbc.command_runner ssh_exit_255_conflation_dissolution rejects stderr-sniffing).",

    "RESIDUE, STATED: a connection lost after the shell started but before its began-line crossed also reads Unreached. The native serving apply that retried only idempotent stages is deleted with the sold Spark serving path; remaining consumers are host_privileged_apply and model_snapshot_materialize.",

    "RUNG: found at 1 (mitigatable). Native-serving-arm witnesses that pinned the reading were deleted with the sold Spark serving path. Remaining inhabitance: dag/test/claim/spark/remote_leg_stdout_exact_witness.dag over gunbc.spark.remote_leg_began / model_snapshot_materialize. CEILING 3: an outcome type every remote-effect leg must produce. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER: gunbc.host_command_binding host_command_outcome_of's Unconfirmed arm consuming the same in-band reading, SUFFICIENT FOR no remote-effect consumer to construct a ran-and-refused value from a leg that never began. PROGRESS: spark_remote_run and host_privileged_apply consume gunbc.spark.remote_leg_began. host_command_outcome_of remains.",
